# Extraction

What is taken out of a model's answer. The output contract: exactly one fenced
block whose info string is `logos-kernel`; fences with any other info string (an
example in prose) are ignored. Outside the block, `Summary: …` is the attempt's
account of itself and each `Next: …` line a suggestion for the attempts after it.
Zero blocks, two blocks or an unclosed block is a refusal, never a guess. A
reviewer answers the same way with one `review` block.

## Note
What an extraction found: the block, the summary, the suggestions, or the problem.

## An Extraction has:
    a block, which is Text.
    a summary, which is Text.
    a suggestions, which is Seq of Text.
    a problem, which is Text.

## Note
Whether a line opens a fence with the given info string, and whether it closes one.

## To opensFence (line: Text, info: Text) -> Bool:
    Let t be trim(line).
    Return startsWith(t, "```") and trim(trimChars(t, "`")) is equal to info.

## To closesFence (line: Text) -> Bool:
    Let t be trim(line).
    Return startsWith(t, "```") and trimChars(t, "`") is equal to "".

## Note
The one block of `info` in an answer, and the lines outside every fence.

## To extractBlock (answer: Text, info: Text) -> Extraction:
    Let mutable found be 0.
    Let mutable fence be 0.
    Let mutable body be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable outside be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for line in lines(answer):
        If fence is equal to 0:
            If opensFence(line, info):
                Set found to found + 1.
                Set fence to 1.
            Otherwise:
                If startsWith(trim(line), "```"):
                    Set fence to 2.
                Otherwise:
                    Push trim(line) to outside.
        Otherwise:
            If closesFence(line):
                Set fence to 0.
            Otherwise:
                If fence is equal to 1 and found is equal to 1:
                    Push line to body.
    Let mutable problem be "".
    If fence is equal to 1:
        Set problem to "the ```{info} block is never closed".
    If found is not equal to 1:
        Set problem to "the answer has {found} ```{info} blocks; exactly one is allowed".
    Let mutable summary be "".
    Let mutable next be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for t in outside:
        If startsWith(t, "Summary:"):
            Set summary to trim(removePrefix(t, "Summary:")).
        If startsWith(t, "Next:"):
            Push trim(removePrefix(t, "Next:")) to next.
    If problem is not equal to "":
        Set body to [].
    Return a new Extraction with block trim(join(body, "\n")) and summary summary and suggestions next and problem problem.

## Note
The submission in a model's answer.

## To extractSubmission (answer: Text) -> Extraction:
    Return extractBlock(answer, "logos-kernel").

## Note
The value of a `key: value` line of a block, or the empty text.

## To fieldLine (block: Text, key: Text) -> Text:
    Repeat for line in lines(block):
        If startsWith(trim(line), key + ":"):
            Return trim(removePrefix(trim(line), key + ":")).
    Return "".

## Test: the submission is the one logos-kernel block, with its summary and suggestions

Let x be extractSubmission("I will induct.\n\n```logos-kernel\nTheorem p : goal := by rfl.\n```\n\nSummary: by computation.\nNext: induct on n.\nNext: unfold first.").
Expect that x's problem is equal to "".
Expect that x's block is equal to "Theorem p : goal := by rfl.".
Expect that x's summary is equal to "by computation.".
Expect that x's suggestions is equal to ["induct on n.", "unfold first."].

## Test: other fences are ignored and zero, two or an unclosed block is refused

Expect that (extractSubmission("```lean\ntheorem t : True\n```\n```logos-kernel\nA.\n```"))'s block is equal to "A.".
Expect that (extractSubmission("no code"))'s problem is equal to "the answer has 0 ```logos-kernel blocks; exactly one is allowed".
Expect that (extractSubmission("```logos-kernel\nA.\n```\n```logos-kernel\nB.\n```"))'s block is equal to "".
Expect that (extractSubmission("```logos-kernel\nTheorem p."))'s problem is equal to "the ```logos-kernel block is never closed".

## Test: a review block's fields are read by name

Let x be extractBlock("```review\nverdict: faithful\nparaphrase: 0 + n = n\nissues: none\n```", "review").
Expect that fieldLine(x's block, "verdict") is equal to "faithful".
Expect that fieldLine(x's block, "paraphrase") is equal to "0 + n = n".

## Test: a second block is refused whatever is in it

For all booleans second:
    Let mutable answer be "```logos-kernel\nA.\n```".
    If second:
        Set answer to answer + "\n```logos-kernel\nB.\n```".
    Expect that ((extractSubmission(answer))'s problem is equal to "") is equal to (not second).
